clark: Whoa, I got a long text message from a girl named Claire.
clark: I wonder who she is.
claire: Clark, I've been trying to contact you for the past month and it's been impossible for me.
claire: I've knocked your door and no one opened, I called you several times and no one answered even though I know you're there.
claire: I'm not in a great mental health mood and you knew that. This silence treatment doesn't do any well to me.
claire: The best solution is that we break up.
clark: Oh, right. I had a girlfriend
claire: I still remember when you used to take to the movies or dinner. I was so happy to share my life with with you.
clark: Tch, whatever.
claire: I was so happy that I actually was going to propose marriage to you. I already had the rings. I guess I'll give them to my sister.
claire: I don't wish you any bad, Clark. I just hope that you can think about your actions and become a better partner for the next person that stumbles upon you.
claire: Best of luck, Claire.
clark: What a wasteful long text. She can go if she wants. She propably was cheating on me
clark: She even says that she was gonna propose marriage. As if I have time for that
clark: Oh wait, I have another text message. It's from a dude called Bob
bob: Man, where the hell are you? You haven't been going to work for the past month.
bob: I've been covering your back ever since. The boss thinks you're sick
bob: I can only help you so much. Please come back on at least call me so you know you're alive.
clark: Oh, yeah. I worked as a salesman.
clark: I absolutely hated that job. They were planning on firing me. They never said anything about that, but I knew it.
clark: I bougth a new game.
clark: I love this console. It's the first console that lets me buy games online.
clark: I don't even have to go outside
clark: This new game is called "SpaceRun"
clark: I don't know if it's gonna be good.
clark: I only bought it because it was on sale
